# Cloudflare Pages reads this file; it is never served.
#
# Everything here is a hand-edited file that changes when you publish, and the
# whole site is five files, so there is nothing worth caching hard. no-cache
# does NOT mean "download every time" — the browser still asks, and gets a
# cheap 304 back when nothing changed. What it buys you is never again seeing
# a stale build and wondering whether the publish worked.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
